\"This collection opens with the death of Ayelet Tsabari's father when she was a nine-year-old girl. His passing left her feeling rootless, devastated, and driven to question her complex identity as an Israeli of Yemeni descent in a country that suppressed and devalued her ancestors' traditions. In The \"Art of Leaving, Ayelet tells her story, from her early love of writing and words, to her rebellion during her mandatory service in the Israeli army. She travels from Israel to New York, to Canada, Thailand, and India, falling in and out of love with countries, men and women, drugs and alcohol, running away from responsibilities and refusing to settle in one place.","thumbnailUrl":"https://books.google.com/books/content?id=D8WrtwEACAAJ&printsec=frontcover&img=1&zoom=1&source=gbs_api","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"essayistic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"essay\"","catalog text contains \"essays\"","catalog text contains \"criticism\"","literature/criticism subject or topic"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":28,"criticalRenown":68,"controversy":8,"llmAffinity":57,"affinityResidual":-17.11,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.82,"controversy":0.72,"llmAffinity":0.2},"tags":{"craft":"prose-style","evidence":"personal-experience","stance":"elegy"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"displaySummary":"In The \"Art of Leaving, Ayelet tells her story, from her early love of writing and words, to her rebellion during her mandatory service in the Israeli army. She travels from Israel to New York, to Canada, Thailand, and India, falling in and out of love with countries, men and women, drugs and alcohol, running away from responsibilities and refusing to settle in one place.","primarySubject":"Biography","primaryTopic":"Disease, Epidemics & Drugs","subjectEvidence":{"p